From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] statusbar: reach the hotspot state through the internet indicator

SignalStrengthIndicator asks wirelessStatus.hotspotSSID whether the
internet indicator's mobile data icon stands in for it, but wirelessStatus
is an id inside InternetIndicator.qml and does not exist here. On mobile
data the binding throws ("ReferenceError: wirelessStatus is not
defined"), visible keeps its default, and the status bar shows the
signal strength icon next to the internet indicator's mobile data icon:
two antennas. Use the internet indicator's wirelessStatus property.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
diff --color -ru a/components/mobileshell/qml/statusbar/indicators/SignalStrengthIndicator.qml b/components/mobileshell/qml/statusbar/indicators/SignalStrengthIndicator.qml
--- a/components/mobileshell/qml/statusbar/indicators/SignalStrengthIndicator.qml	2026-11-19 13:11:24.184230238 +0900
+++ b/components/mobileshell/qml/statusbar/indicators/SignalStrengthIndicator.qml	2026-11-19 13:11:24.193292829 +0900
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
         source: MobileShell.SignalStrengthInfo.icon
 
         // don't show mobile indicator icon if the networkmanager one is already showing
-        visible: (!isInternetIndicatorMobileData || wirelessStatus.hotspotSSID.length !== 0) && MobileShell.SignalStrengthInfo.showIndicator
+        visible: (!isInternetIndicatorMobileData || internetIndicator.wirelessStatus.hotspotSSID.length !== 0) && MobileShell.SignalStrengthInfo.showIndicator
     }
 
     PlasmaComponents.Label {
